# html-template-lab/todo-components — EAV port (apps/html-template-lab/modules/todo-components).
#
# Reusable HTML/SSX components for the console-rendered todo dashboard: a
# component-level htmlTemplate plus a hydration operation. Dynamic holes inside
# the html body only read the operation's hydrate-argument values — the component
# has no request, console, persistence, or todo-domain access; all dynamic
# content arrives through operation inputs forwarded into bare HTML holes.
# (v0.1 `html template`/`html body template`/`html.hydrate.X` -> EAV
# `is htmlTemplate`/`body html`/`html.render arg template HtmlTemplate X`.)

appHtmlTemplateLabTodoComponents is module
appHtmlTemplateLabTodoComponents path apps.htmlTemplateLab.todoComponents
appHtmlTemplateLabTodoComponents imports html standard.html
appHtmlTemplateLabTodoComponents exports renderTodoListFragment
appHtmlTemplateLabTodoComponents purpose "Reusable HTML components for the console-rendered todo dashboard"
appHtmlTemplateLabTodoComponents invariant "Dynamic holes inside html body templates only read hydrate argument values"

HtmlFragment is alias
HtmlFragment for String
HtmlFragment purpose "A rendered, escaped HTML fragment composed into pages"

HtmlTemplate is alias
HtmlTemplate for String
HtmlTemplate purpose "A named html template hydrated by html.render"

# TodoListTemplate: render a fixed three-row ordered todo list as an HTML
# fragment. Renders exactly three rows; dynamic collection rendering is future
# work (v0.1 carried these as `purpose`/`guarantee`; htmlTemplate takes `body`).
TodoListTemplate is htmlTemplate
TodoListTemplate body html
  <section class="todo-list-region" aria-label="Todo list">
    <ol class="todo-list">
      <li class="{{firstTodoClassName}}">
        <span class="todo-title">{{firstTodoTitleText}}</span>
        <span class="todo-status">{{firstTodoStatusText}}</span>
      </li>
      <li class="{{secondTodoClassName}}">
        <span class="todo-title">{{secondTodoTitleText}}</span>
        <span class="todo-status">{{secondTodoStatusText}}</span>
      </li>
      <li class="{{thirdTodoClassName}}">
        <span class="todo-title">{{thirdTodoTitleText}}</span>
        <span class="todo-status">{{thirdTodoStatusText}}</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

renderTodoListFragment is operation
renderTodoListFragment in firstTodoTitleText String
renderTodoListFragment in firstTodoStatusText String
renderTodoListFragment in firstTodoClassName String
renderTodoListFragment in secondTodoTitleText String
renderTodoListFragment in secondTodoStatusText String
renderTodoListFragment in secondTodoClassName String
renderTodoListFragment in thirdTodoTitleText String
renderTodoListFragment in thirdTodoStatusText String
renderTodoListFragment in thirdTodoClassName String
renderTodoListFragment out HtmlFragment
renderTodoListFragment async no
renderTodoListFragment memory heap no
renderTodoListFragment purpose "Hydrate the reusable fixed three-row todo list component from explicit caller inputs"
renderTodoListFragment invariant "All dynamic content arrives through operation inputs forwarded into bare HTML holes"
renderTodoListFragment do hydrateTodoList
renderTodoListFragment return todoListFragment

hydrateTodoList is call
hydrateTodoList in renderTodoListFragment
hydrateTodoList invokes html.render
hydrateTodoList arg template HtmlTemplate TodoListTemplate
hydrateTodoList arg firstTodoClassName String firstTodoClassName
hydrateTodoList arg firstTodoTitleText String firstTodoTitleText
hydrateTodoList arg firstTodoStatusText String firstTodoStatusText
hydrateTodoList arg secondTodoClassName String secondTodoClassName
hydrateTodoList arg secondTodoTitleText String secondTodoTitleText
hydrateTodoList arg secondTodoStatusText String secondTodoStatusText
hydrateTodoList arg thirdTodoClassName String thirdTodoClassName
hydrateTodoList arg thirdTodoTitleText String thirdTodoTitleText
hydrateTodoList arg thirdTodoStatusText String thirdTodoStatusText
hydrateTodoList out todoListFragment HtmlFragment
